# rule.require.timeless-comments

## .what
comments make full sense to a reader with zero knowledge of the session that produced them. state what IS and its durable why; never react to a conversation

## .the test
strip every temporal or reactive word ("yet", "now", "still", "recently", "we decided", "we deliberately", "as discussed"). does it still stand? no → rewrite to the durable principle

## .example
👎 `// no purpose vocabulary — yet. we deliberately do not declare a purpose enum here`
👍 `// purpose is derived, never stamped: each motion already fixes what happened, so a purpose label is a read, not a fact to store`

## .enforcement
- comment that reacts to a conversation or decision-in-progress = nitpick
- comment that will mislead once the conversation is gone = blocker
